# keepwarm configuration.
#
#   cp config.env.example config.env
#
# config.env is gitignored, so your settings survive a `git pull`. Everything
# below is commented out and shows the default. Any setting can also be
# overridden for a single invocation with a KEEPWARM_ prefix:
#
#   KEEPWARM_MODEL=sonnet ./keepwarm ping

# --- schedule -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Length of Claude Code's usage window, in hours. Only change this if Anthropic
# changes the window length.
#WINDOW_HOURS=5

# Minutes to wait past the window boundary before pinging, to absorb clock skew
# between this machine and Anthropic's servers. Every minute here is a minute of
# the fresh window you don't get to use, so keep it small. If pings come back
# LIMITED in the log, raise it to 5.
#SLACK_MINUTES=2

# Minute of the hour the cron job fires on. Re-run "./keepwarm install" after
# changing this.
#CRON_MINUTE=2

# --- the ping itself ----------------------------------------------------------

# Model used for the keepalive. The usage window is account-wide, so the
# cheapest model opens it just as well as an expensive one. Use an alias
# (haiku / sonnet / opus) or a full model id.
#MODEL="haiku"

# The prompt, and a system prompt that REPLACES Claude Code's default one.
# Overriding the system prompt is what keeps this at a few hundred tokens
# instead of the ~15k a normal Claude Code turn sends.
#PING_PROMPT="ping"
#PING_SYSTEM_PROMPT="You are a keepalive probe. Reply with exactly: ok"

# Transient local failures (contended credentials file, brief network trouble)
# are retried within the same run. Without this a single blip costs a whole hour
# of window, because the next attempt would otherwise be the next hourly tick.
# Rate limits are NOT retried — those mean the window genuinely hasn't expired.
#PING_ATTEMPTS=3
#PING_RETRY_DELAY=20

# --- behaviour ----------------------------------------------------------------

# 1 = if you were already using Claude Code after the window boundary, your own
# messages already opened the new window, so skip the ping and just record it.
# 0 = always ping on schedule.
#SKIP_IF_RECENTLY_ACTIVE=1

# Where Claude Code writes session transcripts; used for the activity check.
#ACTIVITY_DIR="$HOME/.claude/projects"

# --- paths --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Leave empty to auto-detect. Auto-detection checks PATH first, then the copies
# bundled inside the VS Code / Cursor extensions (newest wins, so an extension
# update doesn't break the cron job), then ~/.local/bin, ~/.claude/local,
# ~/.bun/bin, /usr/local/bin and /opt/homebrew/bin.
#CLAUDE_BIN=""

# Days of log history to keep.
#LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=30
